{"wikiid":16645,"langid":"en","namespace":"CATEGORY","title":"Fairphone","revisionid":1428440,"contents_raw":"== Background ==\n\nFairphones are smartphones produced by the Amsterdam-based company, Fairphone. Fairphone designs smartphones with the [link|https:\/\/www.fairphone.com\/en\/story\/|goal of reducing their environmental impact|new_window=true], both in the phone\u2019s manufacturing and its life cycle. Fairphones do not contain [link|https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Conflict_resource|conflict minerals] and are manufactured under fair labor conditions.\n\nFairphones are designed to be repairable\u2014meaning users have their smartphone for as long as possible, reducing [link|https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Electronic_waste|e-waste] and keeping the planet that much healthier. Although the original Fairphone scored a 7\/10 repairability score from iFixit, later models improved dramatically and have been scored 10\/10s:\n\n* [guide|20527|Fairphone 1|new_window=true]: ***7\/10***\n* [guide|52523|Fairphone 2|new_window=true]: ***10\/10***\n* [guide|125573|Fairphone 3|new_window=true]: ***10\/10***\n* [link|https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/News\/55818\/fairphone-4-teardown-if-only-apple-made-phones-like-this|Fairphone 4|new_window=true]: ***10\/10***\n* [link|https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/News\/87664\/fairphone-5-keeping-it-10-10|Fairphone 5|new_window=true]: ***10\/10***\n* [link|https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/News\/111613\/fairphone-6-teardown-proof-phones-dont-have-to-be-disposable|Fairphone 6]: ***10\/10***\n\nThe Fairphone 2\u20136 are the only smartphones iFixit has ever given a 10\/10 repairability score.\n\nFairphone also sells numerous [link|https:\/\/shop.fairphone.com\/en\/spare-parts|spare parts|new_window=true], enabling Fairphone owners to easily fix their own devices. Included in the Fairphone parts repository are replacement displays, batteries, cameras, speakers, etc. Fairphone is also committed to keeping their software [link|https:\/\/www.fairphone.com\/en\/open-source\/?ref=footer|open source|new_window=true] and offering 7 years of software support.\n\n== Identification ==\n\nEach generation varies significantly in form factor. Most Fairphones devices proudly state \"FAIRPHONE\" on the back cover.\n\n{table\n| [image|3198755]\n}\n\nThe Fairphone 1's first production line had no external identification other than the logo of a square with a star silhouette. Later editions state \"First Edition\" on the back cover.\n\n{table\n| [image|3198760]\n}\n\n== Additional Information ==\n\n* [link|http:\/\/fairphone.com\/|Fairphone Official Website|new_window=true]\n* [link|https:\/\/fairphone.zendesk.com\/hc\/en-us|Fairphone Product Support|new_window=true]\n* [document|32863|Fairphone Full Impact Report 2022]\n* [link|https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Fairphone|Wikipedia: Fairphone|new_window=true]","contents_json":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fairphones are smartphones produced by the Amsterdam-based company, Fairphone. Fairphone designs smartphones with the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/www.fairphone.com\/en\/story\/","target":"_blank"}}],"text":"goal of reducing their environmental impact"},{"type":"text","text":", both in the phone\u2019s manufacturing and its life cycle. Fairphones do not contain "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Conflict_resource","target":false}}],"text":"conflict minerals"},{"type":"text","text":" and are manufactured under fair labor conditions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fairphones are designed to be repairable\u2014meaning users have their smartphone for as long as possible, reducing "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Electronic_waste","target":false}}],"text":"e-waste"},{"type":"text","text":" and keeping the planet that much healthier. Although the original Fairphone scored a 7\/10 repairability score from iFixit, later models improved dramatically and have been scored 10\/10s:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","attrs":[],"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fairphone 1","marks":[{"type":"siteLink","attrs":{"kind":"guide","id":"20527","options":"","defaultText":null,"newWindow":true,"href":"\/Teardown\/Fairphone+1+Teardown\/20527"}}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"7\/10","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fairphone 2","marks":[{"type":"siteLink","attrs":{"kind":"guide","id":"52523","options":"","defaultText":null,"newWindow":true,"href":"\/Teardown\/Fairphone+2+Teardown\/52523"}}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"10\/10","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fairphone 3","marks":[{"type":"siteLink","attrs":{"kind":"guide","id":"125573","options":"","defaultText":null,"newWindow":true,"href":"\/Teardown\/Fairphone+3+Teardown\/125573"}}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"10\/10","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/News\/55818\/fairphone-4-teardown-if-only-apple-made-phones-like-this","target":"_blank"}}],"text":"Fairphone 4"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"10\/10","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/News\/87664\/fairphone-5-keeping-it-10-10","target":"_blank"}}],"text":"Fairphone 5"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"text","text":"10\/10","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem",